  "tagline": "Discontinued C++ Bigtable clone on HDFS; development stopped in 2016.",
  "description": "Hypertable was an open-source, C++ implementation of the Bigtable design, positioned in the late 2000s as a faster alternative to HBase, and was used for a while by Baidu. It stored sorted, sparse tables across range servers on top of HDFS or other distributed filesystems and offered an SQL-like HQL interface. Hypertable Inc. wound down and the final release, 0.9.8.11, shipped in March 2016; the GitHub repository has seen no meaningful activity since. It is listed here for historical context only; new projects should look at HBase, Bigtable, Cassandra or ScyllaDB.",
